<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Missing Stripes in Data</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If stripes are missing from the scan patch this can be caused by several reasons.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Possible reasons for missing stripes</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Jerking the sensor during scanning. Try to move the sensor smoothly.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Moving the sensor too fast. Adjust the settings in</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings &gt; Real Time Processing &gt; Maximum</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>point spacing</b></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:italic;"><i>.</i></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Too much light being received in the sensor, either ambient light or direct reflections from the object surface, particularly if it is highly reflective. In this case you will be able to hear an audible warning (beep).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>

